  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to create a sense of stewardship for rhinos among the people that live close to two important rhino habitats (Ujung Kulon National Park and Way Kambas National Park). This will be done by: 1. identifying key villages and schools in the region on the eastern side of UKNP and on the western side of WKNP and obtaining approval from villages and schools leaders to give the books to families and schools; 2. producing illustrations for the book; 3. converting book illustrations to digital image format to facilitate layout of the book and purchasing ISBN and EAN numbers and completing copy-ready design and layout of the book; 4. printing 10,000 copies of the book; 5. transporting the book to the field sites; 6. distributing the book to village families (1,500 books to families around UKNP and 1,500 books to families around WKNP); 7. delivering a conservation message to children in key primary schools that the rhinos are an integral part of each park ecosystem and provide each child a book (3,000 books to 10 schools in UKNP and 3,000 books to 10 schools in WKNP); and 8. transitioning the childrens book program to local conservation partners...&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
